      "country": "FRA",
      "split_group": "unsc-meeting:9143:2022-09-30",
      "output": "The 27 September 2022 Council President’s closing national statement attributed to France does not reflect a unanimous Security Council position. The statement, from Source: S/PV.9138, explicitly outlines France’s position on annexation and support for Ukraine. France rejects Russia’s “sham referendums” in occupied Ukrainian territories, calling them a “farce” with “no legal basis or legitimacy.” It reaffirms that “any annexation of a State’s territory by another State resulting from the use or threat of use of force is a violation of the Charter of the United Nations and international law.” France “will never recognize those illegal annexation attempts by Russia.” The statement also affirms France’s continued support for Ukraine, stating it will “provide Ukraine with the support it needs for as long as is necessary” to ensure “respect for its independence, sovereignty and territorial integrity.” However, the statement does not specify an exact financial pledge.",
